	<key>name</key>
	<string>Aardvark Arg Entry Probe (ticket 06, THROWAWAY)</string>
	<key>description</key>
	<string>Throwaway wayfinder ticket 06 probe: feel the two-step add_id entry flow (category pick, then "title :: description"). Writes into a throwaway aardvark system only. Delete after the ticket closes.</string>
	<key>createdby</key>
	<string>wayfinder ticket 06</string>
	<key>version</key>
	<string>0.0.1</string>
	<key>webaddress</key>
	<string></string>
	<key>disabled</key>
	<false/>
	<key>readme</key>
	<string>PREREQ: run ./setup.sh then ./regen.sh in the prototype directory, then import this file.

Keyword: `avid`. Step 1 is a Script Filter listing the throwaway system's categories (Alfred filters the list). Return descends to step 2, a keyword-less Script Filter that takes one free-text field parsed as `title {SEP} description` and shows a live preview. Return on the preview row runs `aardvark add_id` against the throwaway system, reveals the new folder in Finder, and posts a notification.

SEP is set in this workflow's configuration (default `::`). Change it and re-feel the flow against the seeded titles - several contain hyphens and one contains ` :: ` on purpose.

The connection from step 1 to step 2 has "Don't close Alfred" ticked (vitoclose) so the window does not flicker between steps. If step 2 does not auto-run when you press Return on a category, open the workflow in Alfred and confirm that connection exists.</string>
